# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Control is raw device access plus agent code execution; no robotics middleware is mandated.** Hermes drives the hardware by executing code directly against the granted devices (GPIO/I2C/SPI/serial/video libraries), consistent with its self-exploration. This is the deliberate choice over a ROS2/middleware abstraction: the embodied device is already the trust boundary (there is no microVM here), so the agent runs code on the device itself. A middleware layer MAY be added later per robot but is not required by this role."
msgstr "**Kontrolle ist roher Gerätezugriff plus Ausführung von Agentencode; keine Robotik-Middleware ist vorgeschrieben.** Hermes steuert die Hardware, indem er Code direkt gegen die gewährten Geräte ausführt (GPIO/I2C/SPI/serial/video Bibliotheken), im Einklang mit seiner Selbsterforschung. Dies ist die bewusste Wahl gegenüber einer ROS2/Middleware-Abstraktion: Das verkörperte Gerät ist bereits die Vertrauensgrenze (Es gibt keine microVM hier), so dass der Agent Code auf dem Gerät selbst ausführt. Eine Middleware-Schicht kann später pro Roboter hinzugefügt werden, wird aber von dieser Rolle nicht benötigt."

msgid "**Control plane is exempt.** `web-app-semaphore`, `web-app-keycloak`, `svc-db-postgres`, `svc-db-openldap`, `svc-prx-openresty` and `web-app-gitea` (it holds the inventory repository) declare `enabled: false`, `control: false` and `status: started`, each with a `# nocheck:` reason, so no Semaphore run can cut off its own way back."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Control plane stays up:** ``stop`` and ``start`` refuse an application whose ``services.semaphore.control`` is false, and ``all`` acts on exactly the applications with ``control: true``."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Control plane stays up:** `stop` and `start` refuse an application whose `services.semaphore.control` is false, and `all` acts on exactly the applications with `control: true`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Control-plane exemptions:** ``web-app-semaphore``, ``web-app-keycloak``, ``svc-db-postgres``, ``svc-db-openldap``, ``svc-prx-openresty`` and ``web-app-gitea`` declare ``control: false`` and ``status: started`` with a ``# nocheck:`` reason, so no Semaphore run can cut off its own way back. Shared providers that other roles consume, such as ``web-app-matomo`` or ``web-app-prometheus``, stay out of control as well. In ``web-app-semaphore`` the entry is the Semaphore container itself, so its ``enabled`` stays the container flag."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Control-plane exemptions:** `web-app-semaphore`, `web-app-keycloak`, `svc-db-postgres`, `svc-db-openldap`, `svc-prx-openresty` and `web-app-gitea` declare `control: false` and `status: started` with a `# nocheck:` reason, so no Semaphore run can cut off its own way back. Shared providers that other roles consume, such as `web-app-matomo` or `web-app-prometheus`, stay out of control as well. In `web-app-semaphore` the entry is the Semaphore container itself, so its `enabled` stays the container flag."
msgstr ""

