# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Native OIDC flavor** (`services.sso.flavor: oidc`), not the oauth2-proxy gate: OpenBao speaks OIDC itself, so it follows [`web-app-semaphore`](../../roles/web-app-semaphore/) rather than [`web-app-openproject`](../../roles/web-app-openproject/)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Native OIDC login:** The dashboard signs users in against Keycloak's discovery endpoint, without an oauth2-proxy sidecar."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Native OIDC login:** The dashboard signs users in against Keycloak’s discovery endpoint, without an oauth2-proxy sidecar."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Native OIDC:** Grafana signs in through Keycloak with ``auth.generic_oauth`` and auto-login. The role mapping reads the ``RBAC.GROUP.CLAIM`` claim: the ``administrator`` role group maps to the Admin role, the ``auditor`` role group of ``meta/rbac.yml`` maps to Viewer, and with ``role_attribute_strict`` every other account is refused. The RBAC sync grants and revokes both groups like every other role group; Grafana re-evaluates the role at each login."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Native OIDC:** Grafana signs in through Keycloak with `auth.generic_oauth` and auto-login. The role mapping reads the `RBAC.GROUP.CLAIM` claim: the `administrator` role group maps to the Admin role, the `auditor` role group of `meta/rbac.yml` maps to Viewer, and with `role_attribute_strict` every other account is refused. The RBAC sync grants and revokes both groups like every other role group; Grafana re-evaluates the role at each login."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Native Prometheus metrics** via the `services.prometheus.native_metrics` + `templates/prometheus.yml.j2` contract already used by [`web-app-gitea`](../../roles/web-app-gitea/templates/prometheus.yml.j2), scraped on the internal container port over the role-local docker network."
msgstr "**Native Prometheus Metriken** über die `services.prometheus.native_metrics` + `templates/prometheus.yml.j2` Vertrag bereits genutzt von [`web-app-gitea`](../../roles/web-app-gitea/templates/prometheus.yml.j2), auf dem internen Containeranschluss über dem rollenlokalen Docker-Netzwerk abgekratzt."

msgid "**Native client APIs:** exposes OpenAI-compatible and Anthropic-compatible endpoints."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Native in all editions** (incl. Raw): LDAP \"connections\" sync users, contact groups, roles."
msgstr "**Native in allen Editionen** (incl. Rohöl): LDAP \"connections\" Benutzer synchronisieren, Kontaktgruppen, Rollen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Navigate to Pixelfed Directory:** Once inside the container, navigate to the Pixelfed directory. This is typically the root directory where Pixelfed is installed."
msgstr "**In Pixelfed Directory navigieren:** Einmal im Container, navigieren Sie zum Pixelfed-Verzeichnis. Dies ist in der Regel das Stammverzeichnis, in dem Pixelfed installiert ist."

msgid "**Navigation state in the URL.** The open folder is `?folder=<slug>/<slug>` and the search is `?q=<text>`; both combine with the existing `?iframe=`. Every folder change and search commit is a History API entry, so the browser's and the dashboard's own back and forward controls walk the same history."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Nested host network.** Synapse, Element, coturn, LiveKit, its JWT service and Heisenbridge run in the host network of the nested Docker daemon, so they address each other over `127.0.0.1`; Heisenbridge's homeserver URL and its appservice URL in the registration are set accordingly. Jitsi keeps MDAD's own `matrix-jitsi` network and publishes its web port to the runner."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Nested host network.** Synapse, Element, coturn, LiveKit, its JWT service and Heisenbridge run in the host network of the nested Docker daemon, so they address each other over ``127.0.0.1``; Heisenbridge’s homeserver URL and its appservice URL in the registration are set accordingly. Jitsi keeps MDAD’s own ``matrix-jitsi`` network and publishes its web port to the runner."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Nested keys.** Both flat and nested credential keys are accepted, so e.g. `recaptcha.key` and `recaptcha.secret` remain nested."
msgstr "**Nested Keys.** Sowohl flache als auch verschachtelte Anmeldeschlüssel werden akzeptiert, so z.B. `recaptcha.key` und `recaptcha.secret` verschachtelt bleiben."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Network Configuration**: Includes setup of a dedicated Docker network for MariaDB."
msgstr "**Netzwerkkonfiguration**: Beinhaltet die Einrichtung eines dedizierten Docker-Netzwerks für MariaDB."

msgid "**Network Siblings:** [`templates/config-override.php.j2`](./templates/config-override.php.j2) becomes `data/config-override.php`, which answers `siteUrl` with the onion sibling's base URL when a request arrives on that host, so the OIDC `redirect_uri` EspoCRM derives from `siteUrl` returns the login to the host it started on. `data/config.php` keeps the canonical URL, so the CLI and the clearnet host read it unchanged."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Network Siblings:** ```templates/config-override.php.j2`` <./templates/config-override.php.j2>`__ becomes ``data/config-override.php``, which answers ``siteUrl`` with the onion sibling’s base URL when a request arrives on that host, so the OIDC ``redirect_uri`` EspoCRM derives from ``siteUrl`` returns the login to the host it started on. ``data/config.php`` keeps the canonical URL, so the CLI and the clearnet host read it unchanged."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Network bridges are addons.** Appservice / network bridges (e.g. the Matrix `mautrix` bridges to WhatsApp, Telegram, Signal, Slack, Facebook, Instagram) are addons declared under `meta/addons/` with `mechanism: bridge`, one file per bridged network. Each bridge owns its credentials in [`meta/secrets.yml`](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md) and is `required: false` and disabled by default. The role's former bridge declarations (e.g. `web-app-matrix`'s `vars/bridges.yml`) are absorbed into `meta/addons/`."
msgstr "**Netzwerkbrücken sind Addons.** Appservice / Netzwerkbrücken (z.B. die Matrix `mautrix` Brücken zu WhatsApp, Telegram, Signal, Slack, Facebook, Instagram) sind Addons deklariert unter `meta/addons/` mit `mechanism: bridge`, Eine Datei pro Bridged Network. Jede Brücke besitzt ihre Referenzen in [`meta/secrets.yml`](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md) und ist `required: false` und standardmäßig deaktiviert. Die früheren Brückendeklarationen der Rolle (z.B. `web-app-matrix`s `vars/bridges.yml`) werden absorbiert in `meta/addons/`."

msgid "**Network contract:** the role is served on every network the node runs; the application ports carry ``ports.onion.grafana: false`` and ``ports.onion.grafana_onion: false`` and reach the onion through the vhost only. It declares its CSP in ``meta/csp.yml`` and its limits and storage in ``meta/services.yml``."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Network contract:** the role is served on every network the node runs; the application ports carry `ports.onion.grafana: false` and `ports.onion.grafana_onion: false` and reach the onion through the vhost only. It declares its CSP in `meta/csp.yml` and its limits and storage in `meta/services.yml`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Network registry.** One entry per network with its provider role, sibling-domain derivation, transport (TLS policy, scheme, port), client reachability (browser proxy) and CSP scheme. `clearnet` is implicit and has no provider. `onion` is provided by `svc-net-tor`, derives `<sub>.<node>.onion` from `<sub>.<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>`, serves plain HTTP on port 80 and needs the Tor SOCKS proxy in browsers. `handshake` is reserved and not implemented."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Network siblings**: SuiteCRM sends Keycloak `SITE_URL/saml/acs` as the assertion consumer, and its kernel fills `SITE_URL` from the canonical `site_url` unless the request already carries one. [`templates/site_url.php.j2`](./templates/site_url.php.j2) runs as PHP's `auto_prepend_file` (see [`templates/php.ini.j2`](./templates/php.ini.j2)) and sets `SITE_URL` to the onion sibling's origin when a request arrives on that host, so the assertion returns to the host the login started on. Keycloak lists the assertion consumer of every sibling as a valid redirect URI of the SAML client. Requests on the canonical host and CLI runs keep the canonical `site_url`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Network siblings**: SuiteCRM sends Keycloak ``SITE_URL/saml/acs`` as the assertion consumer, and its kernel fills ``SITE_URL`` from the canonical ``site_url`` unless the request already carries one. ```templates/site_url.php.j2`` <./templates/site_url.php.j2>`__ runs as PHP’s ``auto_prepend_file`` (see ```templates/php.ini.j2`` <./templates/php.ini.j2>`__) and sets ``SITE_URL`` to the onion sibling’s origin when a request arrives on that host, so the assertion returns to the host the login started on. Keycloak lists the assertion consumer of every sibling as a valid redirect URI of the SAML client. Requests on the canonical host and CLI runs keep the canonical ``site_url``."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Network siblings.** Every logical domain of a role expands to one domain per effective network. The clearnet sibling is canonical when present."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**NetworkManager + dnsmasq**. preferred path when NetworkManager is active; configures the NM dnsmasq plugin with a wildcard zone entry."
msgstr "**NetworkManager + dnsmasq**. bevorzugter Pfad, wenn NetworkManager aktiv ist; konfiguriert das NM dnsmasq-Plugin mit einem Platzhalterzoneneintrag."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Networks.** For `implementation: sidecar` or `external`, the MCP container MUST attach to the role's existing `networks.local` subnet and MUST NOT introduce a new top-level network."
msgstr "**Netzwerke.** für `implementation: sidecar` oder `external`, MUSS der MCP-Container an die bestehende Rolle anhängen `networks.local` Subnetz und dürfen kein neues top-level-netzwerk einführen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Neutral choice:** Unlike language‑specific collations, `unicode_ci` works robustly in multilingual contexts without bias."
msgstr "**Neutrale Wahl:** Im Gegensatz zu sprachspezifischen Kollationen, `unicode_ci` arbeitet robust in mehrsprachigen Kontexten ohne Vorurteile."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Never a plain container, and the deploy proves it.** A preflight probes the host for `/dev/kvm` and for each runtime's binary, and selects the strongest runtime that is actually installed; the choice is logged at deploy time. It MUST NOT fall back to a plain `runc` container: unisolated execution of model-generated code is never allowed."
msgstr "**Nie ein einfacher Container, und der Einsatz beweist es.** Ein Preflight prüft den Host für `/dev/kvm` und für jede Laufzeit binär ist und die stärkste Laufzeit auswählt, die tatsächlich installiert ist; die Auswahl wird zur Bereitstellungszeit protokolliert. Es darf nicht in eine Ebene zurückfallen `runc` Container: Unisolierte Ausführung von modellgeneriertem Code ist niemals erlaubt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Never commit your API token to a public repository. Always keep it secure!**"
msgstr "**Legen Sie Ihr API-Token niemals einem öffentlichen Repository zu. Immer sicher!**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Never disable.** Required by almost every app."
msgstr "**Niemals deaktivieren.** Erforderlich von fast jeder App."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Never enable buffering for true WebSocket connections!**   Use `proxy_buffering off;` (as in `ws_generic.conf.j2`) or connections may fail."
msgstr "**Aktivieren Sie niemals das Puffern für echte WebSocket-Verbindungen!** Verwendung `proxy_buffering off;` (wie in `ws_generic.conf.j2`) Verbindungen können fehlschlagen."

msgid "**New Badge**: an application deployed after the host's first-deploy record was created carries a \"New\" badge for `services.dashboard.new_days` days."
msgstr ""

msgid "**New Badge**: an application deployed after the host’s first-deploy record was created carries a “New” badge for ``services.dashboard.new_days`` days."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**New CLI capability:** Automatic resolution of *run_after* dependencies with safe cycle detection simplifies role analysis and automation."
msgstr "**Neue CLI-Fähigkeit:** Automatische Auflösung von *run_after* Abhängigkeiten mit sicherer Zykluserkennung vereinfachen die Rollenanalyse und Automatisierung."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**New and reshaped roles.** *sys-svc-nss* is split out of *sys-hostname*, *web-svc-mirror* serves frontend assets as a privacy proxy, PeerTube becomes clearnet-only, and roles that could not run were deleted rather than repaired. CLI tools install via pip instead of pkgmgr."
msgstr "**Neue und neu gestaltete Rollen.** *sys-svc-nss* ist aufgeteilt aus *sys-hostname*, *web-svc-mirror* dient Frontend-Assets als Datenschutz-Proxy, PeerTube wird clearnet-only, und Rollen, die nicht ausgeführt werden konnten, wurden gelöscht, anstatt repariert. CLI-Tools werden über Pip anstelle von pkgmgr installiert."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**New lint contracts.** Port variables must resolve through lookups, scheduler services must declare *replicas: 1*, and volume-owning stack roles must declare their backup policy. *role_path* is forbidden in shell and command bodies. Deployment-mode defaults, container-inspection resolvers, asynchronous-task rationales and health-check declarations are validated centrally. Hadolint directives and documented *nocheck* exceptions are recognized instead of producing false positives."
msgstr "**Neue Flusenverträge.** Portvariablen müssen über Lookups aufgelöst werden, Schedulerdienste müssen *Replicas: 1* deklarieren und volumenbesessene Stackrollen müssen ihre Backup-Richtlinie deklarieren. *role_path* ist in Shell- und Kommandokörpern verboten. Deployment-Mode-Standards, Container-Inspektions-Resolver, Asynchron-Task-Begründungen und Health-Check-Erklärungen werden zentral validiert. Hadolint-Direktiven und dokumentierte *nocheck*-Ausnahmen werden erkannt, anstatt falsche Positive zu erzeugen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Nextcloud minted a new app password on every run and revoked none.** The name was fixed and managed, so each run that found the stored password rejected added another valid token to the account while every previous one kept full access. The mint is now preceded by a listing and the revocation of every token carrying that name."
msgstr "**Nextcloud hat bei jedem Lauf ein neues App-Passwort geprägt und keines widerrufen.** Der Name wurde behoben und verwaltet, so dass jeder Lauf, bei dem das gespeicherte Passwort abgelehnt wurde, dem Konto ein weiteres gültiges Token hinzufügte, während jeder vorherige Zugriff bestand. Der Minze geht nun eine Auflistung und der Widerruf jedes Tokens mit diesem Namen voraus."

