msgstr "**OIDC Support:** Optionale Integration mit OpenID Connect für die zentrale Authentifizierung Ihrer Dienste."

msgid "**OIDC profile sync:** Every OIDC login overwrites the WordPress first name, last name, display name, email, website and language of the user with the Keycloak claims, so Keycloak stays the source of the profile."
msgstr ""

msgid "**OIDC profile sync:** Zammad requests the ``phone`` and ``address`` scopes (``ZAMMAD_OIDC_SCOPE``), and every OIDC sign-in copies the first name, last name, email, phone, street, postal code, city and country from the claims it carries onto the account (``ZAMMAD_OIDC_PROFILE_CLAIMS``, ``ZAMMAD_OIDC_ADDRESS_FIELDS``). A claim the sign-in does not carry leaves the field unchanged, and an email that another Zammad account already holds is kept with an error in the Rails log."
msgstr ""

msgid "**OIDC profile sync:** Zammad requests the `phone` and `address` scopes (`ZAMMAD_OIDC_SCOPE`), and every OIDC sign-in copies the first name, last name, email, phone, street, postal code, city and country from the claims it carries onto the account (`ZAMMAD_OIDC_PROFILE_CLAIMS`, `ZAMMAD_OIDC_ADDRESS_FIELDS`). A claim the sign-in does not carry leaves the field unchanged, and an email that another Zammad account already holds is kept with an error in the Rails log."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**OIDC provider:** inserts the Keycloak provider into ``oauth_providers``. Idempotent via ``ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, provider) DO UPDATE``."
msgstr "**OIDC-Anbieter:** fügt den Keycloak-Anbieter in ``oauth_providers``. Idempotent via ``ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, provider) DO UPDATE``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**OIDC provider:** inserts the Keycloak provider into `oauth_providers`. Idempotent via `ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, provider) DO UPDATE`."
msgstr "**OIDC-Anbieter:** fügt den Keycloak-Anbieter in `oauth_providers`. Idempotent via `ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, provider) DO UPDATE`."

msgid "**OIDC role gate:** The provider's `email_claim` is a Go template rendered from `templates/oidc/email_claim.j2`. It yields the email only when the groups claim holds the `administrator`, `operator` or `user` role group and the `email_verified` claim is true, so Semaphore refuses the Keycloak sign-in of every other realm account, and of an account with an unverified address, with a missing email claim and returns it to the login page. Semaphore links a Keycloak sign-in to its account by that email."
msgstr ""

msgid "**OIDC role gate:** The provider’s ``email_claim`` is a Go template rendered from ``templates/oidc/email_claim.j2``. It yields the email only when the groups claim holds the ``administrator``, ``operator`` or ``user`` role group and the ``email_verified`` claim is true, so Semaphore refuses the Keycloak sign-in of every other realm account, and of an account with an unverified address, with a missing email claim and returns it to the login page. Semaphore links a Keycloak sign-in to its account by that email."
msgstr ""

msgid "**OIDC role mapping:** Every OIDC login sets the WordPress role from the user's Keycloak role groups; a user without one is a Subscriber."
msgstr ""

msgid "**OIDC role mapping:** Every OIDC login sets the WordPress role from the user’s Keycloak role groups; a user without one is a Subscriber."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**OIDC single sign-on and SMTP:** rendered into ``gitlab.yml`` and an ``smtp_settings.rb`` initializer."
msgstr "**OIDC Single Sign-on und SMTP:** gerendert in ``gitlab.yml`` und ein ``smtp_settings.rb`` Initialisierung."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**OIDC single sign-on and SMTP:** rendered into `gitlab.yml` and an `smtp_settings.rb` initializer."
