msgid "**Patched OAuth2 callback:** The role builds ``gitea_custom`` instead of running ``gitea/gitea`` unchanged. The role `Dockerfile <./files/Dockerfile>`__ compiles the backend from the ``gitea-src`` tarball of the pinned release with every patch in ``GITEA_PATCH_FILES`` applied, and replaces ``/app/gitea/gitea`` in the pinned upstream image. `oauth2/redirect-uri-public-url.patch <./files/patch/oauth2/redirect-uri-public-url.patch>`__ takes the OAuth2 callback URL from the public URL the request arrived on instead of ``ROOT_URL``, so an SSO sign-in started on the onion vhost returns to the onion callback. Drop that patch once a Gitea release carries the change."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Patched OAuth2 callback:** The role builds `gitea_custom` instead of running `gitea/gitea` unchanged. The role [Dockerfile](./files/Dockerfile) compiles the backend from the `gitea-src` tarball of the pinned release with every patch in `GITEA_PATCH_FILES` applied, and replaces `/app/gitea/gitea` in the pinned upstream image. [oauth2/redirect-uri-public-url.patch](./files/patch/oauth2/redirect-uri-public-url.patch) takes the OAuth2 callback URL from the public URL the request arrived on instead of `ROOT_URL`, so an SSO sign-in started on the onion vhost returns to the onion callback. Drop that patch once a Gitea release carries the change."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Path arguments stay in their segment:** A value that fills a ``{placeholder}`` of the contracted path is percent-encoded, and an empty value or one made only of dots is refused, so a call cannot resolve to a path the contract does not name."
msgstr "**Pfadargumente bleiben in ihrem Segment:** Ein Wert, der eine ``{placeholder}`` des kontrahierten Pfades ist prozentcodiert, und ein leerer Wert oder einer, der nur aus Punkten besteht, wird abgelehnt, so dass ein Aufruf nicht zu einem Pfad aufgelöst werden kann, den der Vertrag nicht benennt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Path arguments stay in their segment:** A value that fills a `{placeholder}` of the contracted path is percent-encoded, and an empty value or one made only of dots is refused, so a call cannot resolve to a path the contract does not name."
msgstr "**Pfadargumente bleiben in ihrem Segment:** Ein Wert, der eine `{placeholder}` des kontrahierten Pfades ist prozentcodiert, und ein leerer Wert oder einer, der nur aus Punkten besteht, wird abgelehnt, so dass ein Aufruf nicht zu einem Pfad aufgelöst werden kann, den der Vertrag nicht benennt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Paths that look wrong and are not.** Policies mount at `/openbao/policies/`, because OpenBao parses *every* file under `-config` as server configuration. Storage is `/openbao/file`, not `/openbao/data`: the image pre-chowns only `/openbao/{config,logs,file}` for the non-root `openbao` user, so a volume elsewhere lands root-owned and raft cannot write. `command:` is just `server` — the entrypoint appends `-config` itself, and passing it duplicates the flag."
msgstr "**Wege, die falsch aussehen und es nicht sind.** Policies montieren sich am `/openbao/policies/`, weil OpenBao Parses *alle* Datei unter `-config` als Server-Konfiguration. Lagerung ist `/openbao/file`, nicht `/openbao/data`: das Bild nur Pre-Chowns `/openbao/{config,logs,file}` für die Nicht-Wurzel `openbao` Benutzer, so dass ein Volume woanders root-owned und raft nicht schreiben kann. `command:` ist nur `server` — die Entrypoint-Anhänge `-config` sich selbst, und vorbei es dupliziert die Flagge."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Paths that look wrong and are not.** Policies mount at ``/openbao/policies/``, because OpenBao parses *every* file under ``-config`` as server configuration. Storage is ``/openbao/file``, not ``/openbao/data``: the image pre-chowns only ``/openbao/{config,logs,file}`` for the non-root ``openbao`` user, so a volume elsewhere lands root-owned and raft cannot write. ``command:`` is just ``server`` — the entrypoint appends ``-config`` itself, and passing it duplicates the flag."
msgstr "**Wege, die falsch aussehen und es nicht sind.** Policies montieren sich am ``/openbao/policies/``, weil OpenBao Parses *alle* Datei unter ``-config`` als Server-Konfiguration. Lagerung ist ``/openbao/file``, nicht ``/openbao/data``: das Bild nur Pre-Chowns ``/openbao/{config,logs,file}`` für die Nicht-Wurzel ``openbao`` Benutzer, so dass ein Volume woanders root-owned und raft nicht schreiben kann. ``command:`` ist nur ``server`` — die Entrypoint-Anhänge ``-config`` sich selbst, und vorbei es dupliziert die Flagge."

msgid "**Pause and resume:** ``app-control --config <file> stop|start <application_id>|all`` runs ``compose down`` and ``compose up -d`` in compose mode, and scales every service of the stack to 0 replicas or redeploys the rendered stack in swarm mode. The application’s own ``*.infinito.nexus`` timer stops and starts with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Pause and resume:** `app-control --config <file> stop|start <application_id>|all` runs `compose down` and `compose up -d` in compose mode, and scales every service of the stack to 0 replicas or redeploys the rendered stack in swarm mode. The application's own `*.infinito.nexus` timer stops and starts with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page.** While an application is paused, nginx answers every one of its vhosts with HTTP 503 and a page that shows an animation of a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, states that the service is paused, and lists the platform operator's contact channels from `service_provider.contact` (email, Mastodon and the others declared there). The page text is multilingual and managed through the `core` `.po` catalogs."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page:** While an application is paused, nginx answers every one of its vhosts with HTTP 503 and a self-contained page with a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, the paused notice and the contact channels of ``service_provider.contact``. The page is rendered from the ``core`` gettext catalogs in every language they translate, picked from ``Accept-Language``, with English as the fallback."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page:** While an application is paused, nginx answers every one of its vhosts with HTTP 503 and a self-contained page with a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, the paused notice and the contact channels of `service_provider.contact`. The page is rendered from the `core` gettext catalogs in every language they translate, picked from `Accept-Language`, with English as the fallback."
