# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**PromQL interface:** Query and explore metrics via the Prometheus web UI."
msgstr "**PromQL-Schnittstelle:** Abfrage und Erkundung von Metriken über die Prometheus Web-Benutzeroberfläche."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Prometheus ran with no `--query.timeout`**, so a query the adapter abandoned after 15s kept the server busy for its two-minute default, and a range query's point count was unbounded although the response was truncated to 100 rows. The timeout is now derived from `mcp.limits.timeout_seconds`, and `policy.assert_range` refuses a range whose point count exceeds the contract's `result_items`, naming the smallest step that would fit."
msgstr "**Prometheus lief ohne `--query.timeout`**, also eine Abfrage, die der Adapter nach 15s hielt den server wegen seines zweiminütigen standardbetriebs beschäftigt, und die punktzahl einer bereichsabfrage war unbegrenzt, obwohl die antwort auf 100 Zeilen. Das Timeout leitet sich nun von `mcp.limits.timeout_seconds`, und `policy.assert_range` eine Range ablehnt, deren Punktzahl die des Kontrakts übersteigt `result_items`, und nennt den kleinsten Schritt, der passen würde."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Prometheus** metrics support"
msgstr "**Prometheus** Metriken unterstützen"

msgid "**Prompt status:** a successful ``stop`` or ``start`` schedules one run of the webserver health sweep unit named by ``health_service``, ``health_delay_seconds`` after the last such action, through the transient timer ``app-control-health-refresh``; a later action moves the pending run behind it, so a resumed application answers before it is probed and bursts stay below the unit’s start limit. The dashboard’s badge follows one poll after that run. A host without the unit, such as a swarm node that runs no sweep, skips it, and a failure to schedule it is reported on stderr and in the exit code."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Prompt status:** a successful `stop` or `start` schedules one run of the webserver health sweep unit named by `health_service`, `health_delay_seconds` after the last such action, through the transient timer `app-control-health-refresh`; a later action moves the pending run behind it, so a resumed application answers before it is probed and bursts stay below the unit's start limit. The dashboard's badge follows one poll after that run. A host without the unit, such as a swarm node that runs no sweep, skips it, and a failure to schedule it is reported on stderr and in the exit code."
msgstr ""

