# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**RBAC gate:** A user needs the ``agent-user`` role of ``web-app-hermes`` or ``web-app-openclaw``. Open WebUI lists each agent model only to that group, and the broker refuses any other caller with HTTP 403 and stops a running agent of a user who lost the role. Every completion reads the caller’s group membership from Keycloak again, so a grant and a revocation both take effect on the next request."
msgstr "**RBAC-Gatter:** Ein Nutzer braucht die ``agent-user`` Rolle der ``web-app-hermes`` oder ``web-app-openclaw``. Open WebUI listet jedes Agentenmodell nur für diese Gruppe auf, und der Broker lehnt jeden anderen Anrufer mit HTTP ab 403 und stoppt einen Running Agent eines Benutzers, der die Rolle verloren hat. Jede fertigstellung liest die gruppenmitgliedschaft des anrufers aus. Keycloak wieder, so dass sowohl ein Zuschuss als auch ein Widerruf beim nächsten Antrag wirksam werden."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**RBAC gate:** A user needs the `agent-user` role of `web-app-hermes` or `web-app-openclaw`. Open WebUI lists each agent model only to that group, and the broker refuses any other caller with HTTP 403 and stops a running agent of a user who lost the role. Every completion reads the caller's group membership from Keycloak again, so a grant and a revocation both take effect on the next request."
msgstr "**RBAC-Gatter:** Ein Nutzer braucht die `agent-user` Rolle der `web-app-hermes` oder `web-app-openclaw`. Open WebUI listet jedes Agentenmodell nur für diese Gruppe auf, und der Broker lehnt jeden anderen Anrufer mit HTTP ab 403 und stoppt einen Running Agent eines Benutzers, der die Rolle verloren hat. Jede vervollständigung liest die gruppenmitgliedschaft des anrufers aus. Keycloak wieder, so dass sowohl ein Zuschuss als auch ein Widerruf beim nächsten Antrag wirksam werden."

msgid "**RBAC group mapping:** Map the Keycloak groups of the ``administrator``, ``manager``, ``publisher``, ``editor``, ``author`` and ``registered`` roles onto Joomla’s built-in ``Super Users``, ``Manager``, ``Publisher``, ``Editor``, ``Author`` and ``Registered`` user groups on every login."
msgstr ""

msgid "**RBAC group mapping:** Map the Keycloak groups of the `administrator`, `manager`, `publisher`, `editor`, `author` and `registered` roles onto Joomla's built-in `Super Users`, `Manager`, `Publisher`, `Editor`, `Author` and `Registered` user groups on every login."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "**RBAC group → Frappe role mapping:** `ERPNEXT_RBAC_ROLE_GRANTS` maps `administrator` → `System Manager`, `manager` → `{Sales, Purchase, Stock, Accounts} User` and `customer` → `Customer`. With SSO or LDAP, [`files/python/apply/rbac_roles.py`](./files/python/apply/rbac_roles.py) runs as an RBAC hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) inside the backend container at every deploy and on its timer: it renames the account of a member whose address changed, found by its `keycloak` or `directory` `User Social Login` row, to the new address, creates the members of the three role groups, grants their roles, re-enables a disabled member and withdraws these roles from every other account the directory owns, as [RBAC scope](#rbac-scope) describes. The Administrator, Guest, the API bot and the platform administrator (`ERPNEXT_RBAC_PROTECTED_USERS`) are never demoted or disabled. The Social Login Key denies sign-ups, so a Keycloak user outside the role groups cannot create an account. With `svc-db-openldap` deployed, a group change in Keycloak or LDAP takes effect within one timer interval, or earlier at the user's next Keycloak sign-in (see below); without a directory the role groups are inventory grants that the next deploy applies."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "**RBAC group → Frappe role mapping:** ``ERPNEXT_RBAC_ROLE_GRANTS`` maps ``administrator`` → ``System Manager``, ``manager`` → ``{Sales, Purchase, Stock, Accounts} User`` and ``customer`` → ``Customer``. With SSO or LDAP, ```files/python/apply/rbac_roles.py`` <./files/python/apply/rbac_roles.py>`__ runs as an RBAC hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ inside the backend container at every deploy and on its timer: it renames the account of a member whose address changed, found by its ``keycloak`` or ``directory`` ``User Social Login`` row, to the new address, creates the members of the three role groups, grants their roles, re-enables a disabled member and withdraws these roles from every other account the directory owns, as `RBAC scope <#rbac-scope>`__ describes. The Administrator, Guest, the API bot and the platform administrator (``ERPNEXT_RBAC_PROTECTED_USERS``) are never demoted or disabled. The Social Login Key denies sign-ups, so a Keycloak user outside the role groups cannot create an account. With ``svc-db-openldap`` deployed, a group change in Keycloak or LDAP takes effect within one timer interval, or earlier at the user’s next Keycloak sign-in (see below); without a directory the role groups are inventory grants that the next deploy applies."
msgstr ""

msgid "**RBAC lock.** Tiles are never hidden. A small lock in the tile's bottom-right corner marks an application the visitor may not open. The lock is a hint only; the SSO gate and the application stay the authority."
msgstr ""

msgid "**RBAC policies:** One MinIO policy per RBAC group path (``administrator``, ``readwrite``, ``readonly``). OIDC logins pick them up through the groups claim, and the LDAP variant attaches each policy to its ``web-app-minio-<role>`` group under the roles OU."
msgstr ""

msgid "**RBAC policies:** One MinIO policy per RBAC group path (`administrator`, `readwrite`, `readonly`). OIDC logins pick them up through the groups claim, and the LDAP variant attaches each policy to its `web-app-minio-<role>` group under the roles OU."
msgstr ""

msgid "**RBAC reconcile:** [`files/php/apply/rbac_sync.php`](./files/php/apply/rbac_sync.php) runs as an RBAC hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer (`tasks/06_rbac.yml`). It imports the directory members with `snipeit:ldap-sync` when LDAP is on, then `administrator` members get the `superuser` permission, every member joins the `web-app-snipe-it-user` permission group (also the LDAP default group), accounts outside both groups lose `superuser`, `admin` and that group. Members without an account are created. The bootstrap administrator and the MCP account are never changed."
msgstr ""

