msgid "**Reboot guard on Arch:** After the upgrade, ``arch.yml`` checks whether the running kernel loads modules and ``/usr/lib/modules`` holds a ``modules.dep`` for other kernels but not for it, before any later role restarts Docker. When it does not, the role reboots the host one at a time (``throttle: 1``), waits until ``systemctl is-system-running`` reports ``running`` or ``degraded``, re-reads the booted kernel, checks again and fails when the booted kernel still has no ``modules.dep``. It fails with “Reboot required” instead of rebooting when ``services.update.reboot.enabled`` is ``false``, in check mode, when ``svc-net-wireguard`` brought its mesh up with ``wg-quick`` in the same play, and when the host shares its boot id with the Ansible controller (local connection, SSH to itself, or a controller container on the host). Containers (``DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER``) skip the check."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reboot guard on Arch:** After the upgrade, `arch.yml` checks whether the running kernel loads modules and `/usr/lib/modules` holds a `modules.dep` for other kernels but not for it, before any later role restarts Docker. When it does not, the role reboots the host one at a time (`throttle: 1`), waits until `systemctl is-system-running` reports `running` or `degraded`, re-reads the booted kernel, checks again and fails when the booted kernel still has no `modules.dep`. It fails with \"Reboot required\" instead of rebooting when `services.update.reboot.enabled` is `false`, in check mode, when `svc-net-wireguard` brought its mesh up with `wg-quick` in the same play, and when the host shares its boot id with the Ansible controller (local connection, SSH to itself, or a controller container on the host). Containers (`DOCKER_IN_CONTAINER`) skip the check."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reboot switch:** ``services.update.reboot.enabled`` defaults to ``false``. Switch it on per host in the ``applications`` block of its ``host_vars``; a ``group_vars`` value is replaced by any ``host_vars`` ``applications`` block:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reboot switch:** `services.update.reboot.enabled` defaults to `false`. Switch it on per host in the `applications` block of its `host_vars`; a `group_vars` value is replaced by any `host_vars` `applications` block:"
