# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A ``type: volume`` entry may set ``nfs: false`` to opt out of the swarm NFS rewrite: the volume then stays a plain node-local named volume even when ``storage.backend`` is ``nfs`` (e.g. gitaly repository storage, which upstream forbids on NFS). Any other ``nfs`` value (absent, ``true``, or the uid/gid/mode dict consumed by the NFS subdir pre-creation) keeps the rewrite."
msgstr "A ``type: volume`` Eintrag kann eingestellt werden ``nfs: false`` Opt-out aus dem Schwarm NFS rewrite: das Volume bleibt dann ein einfaches Node-local benanntes Volume, auch wenn ``storage.backend`` ist ``nfs`` (z. B. gitaly repository storage, was Upstream NFS verbietet). andere ``nfs`` Wert (abwesend), ``true``, oder das uid/gid/mode dict, das von der NFS subdir pre-creation verbraucht wird, hält das Umschreiben."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A ``version`` that names its own upstream in an ``update:`` block belongs to :mod:`utils.update.source` and is not collected here."
msgstr "A ``version`` die ihren eigenen Upstream in einem ``update:`` Block gehört zu :mod:`utils.update.source` und wird hier nicht gesammelt."

msgid "A `container` hook pipes its script into a command inside the application's container, for applications whose image ships a scripting runtime. A `host` hook runs its script with the node's Python beside its modules and reaches the container through `$RBAC_SYNC_CONTAINER_BIN exec ... $RBAC_SYNC_CID`, for applications that only expose a CLI or an HTTP API inside the container. A hook runs on the node of the one container it names and reaches nothing else: in swarm no `ports.local` port is published, so an application whose hook acts on its database cannot also call its own HTTP API from there. Such work runs at deploy time inside the application's network namespace, as [web-app-peertube](../web-app-peertube/README.md) creates its accounts, and the hook keeps the SQL."
