msgstr ""

msgid "A deploy with the mail provider switched off starts the local postfix relay on `127.0.0.1:25` (`tasks/enable.yml:37`), but a mail server an earlier deploy started on the same host keeps running and publishes port 25 (and 465) on `0.0.0.0`, so postfix fails with `fatal: bind 127.0.0.1 port 25: Address already in use` and the deploy stops at \"Ensure the local relay is listening\". Measured in the IAM B2 compose round of 2026-11-01 with `web-app-stalwart` left running from the previous round (`/tmp/compose-deploy-iam-18.log:64181`); the same holds on a production host that switches email off after running Stalwart, because the app-control of the new round does not cover the old provider (`app-control stop web-app-stalwart` answers \"not under app control\"). Options: before starting postfix, detect a listener on port 25 and fail with a message naming the running mail server and how to stop it, or stop the previous provider's stack when its application leaves the inventory. Tracked in issue #1333."
msgstr ""

