msgid "A model that serves agents declares its context window in tokens: `context` on an `AI_LOCAL_MODELS` entry or on a `services.litellm.remote_models` entry. LiteLLM sends it to Ollama as `num_ctx` and publishes it as `model_info.max_input_tokens`, and the broker writes it into the agent config as Hermes `model.context_length` and OpenClaw `contextWindow`. Without it Ollama truncates the agent's prompt to its own default window and the agents assume windows of their own."
msgstr "Ein Modell, das Agenten bedient, deklariert sein Kontextfenster in Token: `context` in einem `AI_LOCAL_MODELS` Eingang oder auf einem `services.litellm.remote_models` Eintrag. LiteLLM schickt es an Ollama als `num_ctx` und veröffentlicht es als `model_info.max_input_tokens`, und der Broker schreibt es in die Agent Config als Hermes `model.context_length` und OpenClaw `contextWindow`. ohne Ollama verkürzt die Eingabeaufforderung des Agenten auf sein eigenes Standardfenster und die Agenten übernehmen eigene Fenster."

msgid "A model vendor (`flavour: model-vendor`) also lists the agent `runtimes` it serves and its `login_hosts`. A workspace with `model_access: login` adds exactly these hosts to its egress, and only for a runtime the vendor names; in gateway mode they stay closed, and a deny rule of the agent's firewall role removes any of them in both modes; every egress target is compared lowercase and without a trailing dot, and L08 refuses any other spelling. Lint L08 accepts only exact login host names and refuses hosts that serve user content (`claude.ai`, `chatgpt.com`). Codex signed in with a ChatGPT account talks to `chatgpt.com`, which also serves the account's conversations and file uploads, so `openai.yml` does not list it: a login-mode Codex VM works only with an OpenAI API login until the proxy can admit a single path of that host."
