# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Ansible forks a fresh worker process for every task. The in-process cache inside `get_merged_applications` therefore never survives from one task to the next, and every task that touches the lookup would render the full tree again (about 16 to 23 seconds per task on a CI runner, measured on the workspace jobs)."
msgstr "Ansible forkt für jede Aufgabe einen frischen Worker-Prozess. Der In-Prozess-Cache im Inneren `get_merged_applications` Daher überlebt nie von einer Aufgabe zur nächsten, und jede Aufgabe, die den Lookup berührt, würde den vollen Baum wiedergeben (ca. 16 bis 23 Sekunden pro Aufgabe bei einem CI-Läufer, gemessen an den Workspace-Jobs)."

msgid "Ansible forks a fresh worker process per task, so the in-process `_MERGED_APPLICATIONS_CACHE` and `_MERGED_USERS_CACHE` start empty in every worker. The constructor stage renders once and parks each payload plus its cache key in the host facts named by `APPLICATIONS_RENDERED_FACT` and `USERS_RENDERED_FACT`; every later worker inherits those facts at fork time and `get_merged_applications` / `get_merged_users` serve them instead of rendering. Ansible-free at import time like the rest of the package."
msgstr ""

