msgid "Declare it under `cache:` in a `meta/networks.yml`, then run `make dotenv` followed by `make cache-apply`. That file is the single point of truth; the Nexus repo, the leaf cert, the nginx server block, the `extra_hosts` entries, `pip.conf`, `.npmrc` and the apt sources are all derived from it. `make dotenv` renders them, `make cache-apply` installs them into the running stack: it creates the Nexus proxy repositories, issues the frontend's leaf certificates, copies the upstream map onto the path the frontend mounts and reloads it. Recreate the checkout's runner with `make compose-up` afterwards so the new DNS hijacks reach it."
