msgid "Destinations in `NETWORK_INTERNAL_CIDRS`, link-local, multicast and limited broadcast are not egress and stay direct under `all`, except DNS. Port 53 and 853, UDP and TCP, reach only the `resolvers` set: loopback, the container DNS host and the local subnets of the roles deployed on the node, where role resolvers such as svc-dns-unbound live. The container address pools are not in it, so a LAN resolver inside a pool (`172.30.0.53` in `172.16.0.0/12`) cannot answer for names Tor should resolve. The guard runs before the internal accept, IPv6 DNS is dropped outright, and the nat chain returns TCP DNS so it meets the drop instead of the TransPort. The deploy refuses a `networks.internet.dns` inside the resolver set, because every process could reach it."
msgstr ""

