# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Every desk list page logs one `Executing inline event handler violates the following Content Security Policy directive 'script-src-attr 'self''` per page menu entry (measured: 17 `a.grey-link[onclick]` on `/desk/build/todo`, 16 on `/desk/users/user`, 49 console errors after two list pages). Cause: Frappe renders the page menu entries with `onClick=\"return false;\"` (`frappe/public/js/frappe/ui/page.js:564,577` at v16.50.0) and `meta/csp.yml` allows no inline handler, so a click on such an entry also follows its `href=\"#\"`. Options: allow that one handler through `'unsafe-hashes'` plus its hash in `script-src-attr`, or accept the blocked handler since the menu actions run through jQuery handlers."
