# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Taiga redirects `/` to the public `/discover` showcase, which renders a bare Login link but not the OIDC entry point; only `/login` binds the SSO directive (see the note in [`files/playwright/_shared.js`](./files/playwright/_shared.js)). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga's SSO button. Taiga's AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through `ng-click` / `tg-nav` / `ui-sref` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) therefore declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local `test-login-oidc.js` and `test-login-native.js` specs, which enter at `/login` and log out through Taiga's own control."
msgstr "Taiga Redirects `/` für die Öffentlichkeit `/discover` Schaufenster, das einen bloßen Login-Link darstellt, aber nicht den OIDC-Eingangspunkt; nur `/login` bindet die SSO-Richtlinie (siehe den Hinweis in) [`files/playwright/_shared.js`](./files/playwright/_shared.js). Die freigegebenen Personas treten immer am Website-Root ein, so dass sie niemals den SSO-Button von Taiga erreichen können. Taigas AngularJS-Shell zeigt zusätzlich Logout nur durch `ng-click` / `tg-nav` / `ui-sref` Richtlinien, die der generische In-App-Logout-Helfer nicht aktivieren kann. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) erklärt daher `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` und `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; die äquivalenten Reisen werden durch die rollenlokale `test-login-oidc.js` und `test-login-native.js` Specs, die bei `/login` und loggen sich durch Taigas eigene Kontrolle ab."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Taiga redirects ``/`` to the public ``/discover`` showcase, which renders a bare Login link but not the OIDC entry point; only ``/login`` binds the SSO directive (see the note in ```files/playwright/_shared.js`` <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga’s SSO button. Taiga’s AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through ``ng-click`` / ``tg-nav`` / ``ui-sref`` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local ``test-login-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-native.js`` specs, which enter at ``/login`` and log out through Taiga’s own control."
msgstr "Taiga Redirects ``/`` für die Öffentlichkeit ``/discover`` Schaufenster, das einen bloßen Login-Link darstellt, aber nicht den OIDC-Eingangspunkt; nur ``/login`` bindet die SSO-Richtlinie (siehe Notiz in ```files/playwright/_shared.js`` <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__). The shared personas always enter at the site root, so they can never reach Taiga’s SSO button. Taiga’s AngularJS shell additionally exposes logout only through ``ng-click`` / ``tg-nav`` / ``ui-sref`` directives, which the generic in-app logout helper cannot activate. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the equivalent journeys are driven by the role-local ``test-login-oidc.js`` and ``test-login-native.js`` specs, which enter at ``/login`` und loggen sich durch Taigas eigene Kontrolle ab."

