msgid "The OIDC directory skips the audience check and gives Keycloak tokens without Stalwart scopes access to mail, contacts, calendars and files (``STALWART_OIDC_TOKEN_VALIDATION``). Tokens of the ``stalwart-webui`` client get full access, because the WebUI Application names it as its ``oauthClientId``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The OIDC endpoints under `/realms/` and the static assets under `/resources/` stay public."
msgstr ""

msgid "The OIDC endpoints under ``/realms/`` and the static assets under ``/resources/`` stay public."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The OIDC group path `/roles/web-app-openbao/<role>` already namespaces by application, so an `openbao-` prefix would be redundant, and the repo's other `meta/rbac.yml` files use bare role names."
msgstr "OIDC-Gruppenpfad `/roles/web-app-openbao/<role>` bereits Namespaces nach Anwendung, also ein `openbao-` Präfix wäre überflüssig, und das andere repo `meta/rbac.yml` Dateien verwenden bloße Rollennamen."

msgid "The OIDC login + RBAC paths are covered by ``test-admin-oidc-login.js`` / ``test-rbac-roles.js`` / ``test-multisite-rbac.js``, the profile sync by ``test-profile-sync.js``, the profile lock with its warning on ``profile.php`` and ``user-edit.php`` and against direct form, REST and XML-RPC writes by ``test-profile-lock.js``, the Discourse round-trip by ``test-discourse-roundtrip.js``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The OIDC login + RBAC paths are covered by `test-admin-oidc-login.js` / `test-rbac-roles.js` / `test-multisite-rbac.js`, the profile sync by `test-profile-sync.js`, the profile lock with its warning on `profile.php` and `user-edit.php` and against direct form, REST and XML-RPC writes by `test-profile-lock.js`, the Discourse round-trip by `test-discourse-roundtrip.js`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The OIDC login entry points (`oidc_login`, `sociallogin`, `user_oidc`) are mandatory because they gate SSO login: when one of them is the selected flavor and the system hides the native login form, an un-installed OIDC app leaves the instance with no usable login path. Failing at install time surfaces the version-pin mismatch immediately rather than as a downstream login timeout in the Playwright e2e suite."
msgstr "Die OIDC-Login-Einstiegspunkte (`oidc_login`, `sociallogin`, `user_oidc`) sind obligatorisch, weil sie SSO-Login-Gatter: Wenn einer von ihnen der ausgewählte Geschmack ist und das System das native Anmeldeformular verbirgt, verlässt eine nicht installierte OIDC-App die Instanz ohne nutzbaren Anmeldepfad. Wenn Sie zum Zeitpunkt der Installation ausfallen, wird die Versions-Pin-Mismatch sofort und nicht als nachgelagertes Anmelde-Timeout in der Playwright e2e-Suite angezeigt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The OIDC role's `groups_claim` (JSON-pointer capable) names the claim holding the user's groups; those values resolve against identity groups of `type=external` via group aliases on the auth mount, which carry the policies."
msgstr "Die Rolle der OIDC `groups_claim` (JSON-Zeiger fähig) benennt den Anspruch, der die Gruppen des Benutzers enthält; diese Werte lösen sich mit Identitätsgruppen von `type=external` über Gruppenaliase auf dem Auth-Mount, die die Richtlinien tragen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The OIDC username claim is paired with the LDAP login attribute by design. See [ldap.md](ldap.md) for the LDAP-side rule."
msgstr "Die OIDC-Benutzername-Behauptung wird durch Design mit dem LDAP-Login-Attribut gepaart. Siehe [ldap.md](ldap.md) für die LDAP-Seitenregel."

