msgid "The `auto` alias exists and every other alias still resolves"
msgstr "Die `auto` Alias existiert und jeder andere Alias wird immer noch aufgelöst"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `biber` and `administrator` Playwright personas are gated on `services.sso.enabled`. When SSO is off, [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) renders `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`. Two reasons:"
msgstr "Die `biber` und `administrator` Playwright-Personas sind angeschaltet `services.sso.enabled`. Wenn SSO ausgeschaltet ist, [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) Putz `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` und `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`. Zwei Gründe:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `biber` and `administrator` personas always end on a verified unauthenticated landing via the in-app logout button."
msgstr "Die `biber` und `administrator` Personas enden immer mit einer verifizierten, nicht authentifizierten Landung über den In-App-Logout-Button."

msgid "The `biber` and `administrator` personas are blocked. `meta/services.yml` pins `sso.enabled: false` and `logout.enabled: false`, the Keycloak personas own no PDS account to sign in with, and atmo has no admin surface outside the DID-based moderation. The Playwright suite covers the public appview, the OAuth client metadata and the cron guard instead."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The `biber` persona MUST drive at least one role-specific interaction that a regular end-user would perform (post a message, open a settings tab, browse a content list, submit a form, …). Specs supply this via the `biberInteraction` callback on `runBiberFlow(page, { biberInteraction })`. There is NO generic default. A generic \"click any link\" assertion tests nothing role-specific, so the helper is a no-op until the spec provides a callback."
msgstr "Die `biber` Persona MUSS mindestens eine rollenspezifische Interaktion auslösen, die ein normaler Endbenutzer ausführen würde (Nachrichten posten, Einstellungen öffnen, Inhaltsliste durchsuchen, Formular einreichen, ...). Specs liefern dies über die `biberInteraction` Rückruf auf `runBiberFlow(page, { biberInteraction })`. Es gibt keinen generischen Standard. Eine generische \"Klick auf einen Link\" -Behauptung testet nichts rollenspezifisches, so dass der Helfer ein No-Op ist, bis die Spezifikation einen Rückruf liefert."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The `biber` persona logs in through OIDC without trouble; what it cannot do is log out. Decidim's sign-out is a `data-method` link inside the account dropdown, so the role's own tests navigate to `/users/sign_out` directly rather than clicking a button the shared helper could find."
msgstr "Die `biber` Persona meldet sich ohne Probleme über OIDC an; was es nicht tun kann, ist sich abzumelden. Decidim's Sign-Out ist ein `data-method` Link innerhalb des Account-Dropdowns, so dass die rolleneigenen Tests zu `/users/sign_out` Anstatt direkt auf einen Button zu klicken, könnte der geteilte Helfer finden."

msgid "The `biber` persona passes the oauth2 gate and reaches the dashboard; the `guest` persona is turned away at the gate. The `administrator` persona is blocked in [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2): the gate admits every platform user alike and the dashboard has no admin surface, so an administrator journey would only repeat the biber one."
msgstr ""

msgid "The `biber` persona passes the oauth2 gate when Keycloak is deployed and then the server's native login form; the `guest` persona is turned away at whichever of the two comes first. The `administrator` persona is blocked in [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2): host-login accounts get no render account, and every account in the users file has the same rights, so there is no admin surface to assert."
msgstr ""

