msgid "The checks use the real virtual keys, so they also detect gateway permissions, revoked keys, key budgets and translation failures that a direct provider check cannot detect. Every inference must return nonempty answer text in the expected protocol format without an error payload; an HTTP 200 or reasoning-only response is insufficient. Each inference uses the same configured output-token budget; the number of requests is two per consumer and chat model, plus a Responses API request to `/v1/responses` for each Codex model. Remote requests can incur API charges. `services.litellm.consumer_validation` configures bounded retries: `retries: 2`, `delay: 60` seconds and `max_delay: 120` seconds per wait. HTTP 429 and adapter-wrapped HTTP 5xx responses explicitly reporting a rate limit or cooldown are retried. The validator honors numeric and HTTP-date `Retry-After` headers, waits at least the configured delay, and fails without an early retry when the requested wait exceeds `max_delay`. Recognized daily-quota exhaustion, authentication, credit and other permanent errors are not retried. Exhausted retries still fail deployment. Each result records attempts and seconds waited. Provider daily quotas remain shared across consumers; repeatedly redeploying a free model consumes that quota even when gateway keys are valid."
msgstr ""

