msgid "The sample line is the in-band half of that: it carries memory, disk and the three PSI resources plus the uninterruptible-process count, so a cut that happens anyway can still be attributed afterwards from the step log alone."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox (`allowWrite`, `denyRead`, `allowedDomains`, see [sandbox.md](sandbox.md)) bounds every write, every read, and every outbound connection. `deny` rules block destructive patterns unconditionally; `ask` rules force operator review on every mutating `gh`/`docker`/`git commit`/`Skill(update-config*)` invocation. The wildcard does **not** loosen any existing guardrail; it only drops the per-shape workarounds."
msgstr "Die Sandbox (`allowWrite`, `denyRead`, `allowedDomains`, siehe [sandbox.md](sandbox.md)) Sie grenzt jedes Schreiben, jedes Lesen und jede ausgehende Verbindung ein. `deny` Regeln blockieren destruktive Muster bedingungslos; `ask` Regeln erzwingen Betreiberüberprüfung bei jeder Mutation `gh`/`docker`/`git commit`/`Skill(update-config*)` Invokation. Die Wildcard macht **nicht** Lösen Sie alle vorhandenen Leitplanken; es lässt nur die pro-Form Workarounds fallen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox `denyRead: ~/.gnupg` rule blocks GPG access by design; agent commands must never touch private key material. This env override removes the resulting signing failure without weakening the credential-path protection. Agent-authored commits land unsigned; the `Co-Authored-By` trailer documents authorship."
msgstr "Die Sandbox `denyRead: ~/.gnupg` Regel blockiert den GPG-Zugriff durch Design; Agentenbefehle dürfen niemals privates Schlüsselmaterial berühren. Diese Env-Override entfernt den daraus resultierenden Signierfehler, ohne den Credential-Pfad-Schutz zu schwächen. Agent-authored verpflichtet Land unsigned; die `Co-Authored-By` Trailer Dokumente Urheberschaft."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox can connect to any Unix-domain socket on the host. Required so commands like `docker`, `systemctl`, and language servers continue to work; these all communicate over Unix sockets (e.g. `/var/run/docker.sock`)."
msgstr "Die Sandbox kann mit jedem Unix-Domain-Socket auf dem Host verbunden werden. Erforderlich sind Befehle wie `docker`, `systemctl`, und Sprachserver funktionieren weiterhin; diese kommunizieren alle über Unix-Sockets (z.B. `/var/run/docker.sock`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox cannot be escaped through the host daemon"
msgstr "Die Sandbox kann nicht durch den Host-Daemon entkommen"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox has `sandbox.network.allowAllUnixSockets: true` so that normal workflow tools (`docker`, `systemctl`, language servers) continue to work. Any command that reaches `/var/run/docker.sock` can request a container with `-v /:/host --privileged`, which the Docker daemon executes as root and mounts the host filesystem. The sandbox's `allowWrite` does NOT protect against this path because Docker is a trusted service on the other end of the socket."
msgstr "Die Sandbox hat `sandbox.network.allowAllUnixSockets: true` So können normale Workflow-Tools (`docker`, `systemctl`, Sprachserver) weiterarbeiten. Jeder Befehl, der `/var/run/docker.sock` kann einen Container mit `-v /:/host --privileged`, die der Docker-Daemon als root ausführt und das Host-Dateisystem mountet. Die Sandbox ist `allowWrite` schützt NICHT vor diesem Pfad, da Docker ein vertrauenswürdiger Dienst am anderen Ende des Sockets ist."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The sandbox is activated unconditionally via `\"sandbox\": { \"enabled\": true }`. This means filesystem and network restrictions below are enforced **at every session**, not only when the operator manually switches into sandbox permission mode. The OS-level sandbox is the source of truth for what commands may read, write, and reach over the network; the `allow`/`ask`/`deny` permission lists remain in force as a second line of defence for policy concerns the OS cannot express (e.g. requiring confirmation before publishing a commit)."
msgstr "Die Sandbox wird bedingungslos aktiviert über `\"sandbox\": { \"enabled\": true }`. Dies bedeutet, dass Dateisystem- und Netzwerkbeschränkungen unten **bei jeder Sitzung** durchgesetzt werden, nicht nur, wenn der Bediener manuell in den Sandbox-Berechtigungsmodus wechselt. Die Sandbox auf OS-Ebene ist die Quelle der Wahrheit für das, was Befehle lesen, schreiben und über das Netzwerk erreichen können. `allow`/`ask`/`deny` Genehmigungslisten bleiben in Kraft, da eine zweite Verteidigungslinie für politische Bedenken besteht, die das Betriebssystem nicht äußern kann (z. B. eine Bestätigung vor der Veröffentlichung eines Commits)."

msgid "The sandbox's `denyRead` list (`~/.aws`, `~/.config/gcloud`, `~/.docker/config.json`, `~/.git-credentials`, `~/.gnupg`, `~/.kube`, `~/.netrc`, and the default private keys under `~/.ssh`) is the primary mechanism that prevents the agent from reading host credentials. Every credential store an operator uses on the host is assumed to be covered, **with the documented exceptions of the rest of `~/.ssh`** (see Assumption 10) **and `~/.config/gh`**, which `gh` needs on every call."
msgstr ""

msgid "The scan is a stdlib line parse rather than a YAML load. This module is imported by the ``.env`` generator, which runs on the bare bootstrap python before any dependency is installed, so it must not reach PyYAML - directly or through ``utils.cache.yaml``. Only the ``image:`` value is needed and it is always a plain scalar, so a line match is sufficient; a value carrying Jinja is skipped, because its registry is not knowable before the templar runs."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scan is cached behind a fresh list, because one source message is scanned once per target language and callers may sort or trim the result."
msgstr "Der scan wird hinter einer neuen liste zwischengespeichert, da eine quellnachricht einmal pro zielsprache gescannt wird und anrufer das ergebnis sortieren oder schneiden können."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scheduled `🔄 Update versions` pipeline (version bumps and PR open/refresh)."
msgstr "Der geplante `🔄 Update versions` Pipeline (Version Bumps und PR Open/Refresh)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scheduled update workflow MUST be able to reuse the same discovery logic in update mode. Version bumps MAY update `version`; new addon entries MAY be added with `enabled: false`, `required: false`, and complete `update` metadata."
msgstr "Der geplante Update-Workflow MUSS die gleiche Discovery-Logik im Update-Modus wiederverwenden können. Version Bumps MAY Update `version`; neue Addon-Einträge können hinzugefügt werden mit `enabled: false`, `required: false`, und vollständig `update` Metadaten."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The schema lives at ``meta/networks.yml.overlay`` per provider role, discovered into the service_registry by ``discover_role_services``. Keys:"
msgstr "Das Schema lebt in ``meta/networks.yml.overlay`` pro Anbieterrolle, entdeckt in die service_registry durch ``discover_role_services``. Schlüssel:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The schema rejects a generic URL, a runtime OpenAPI document, free-form GraphQL, a raw SQL tool, an unrestricted bucket, an arbitrary filesystem root, a shell command, a Docker socket, and implicit exposure of every operation an upstream upgrade adds."
msgstr "Das Schema lehnt eine generische URL, ein Runtime OpenAPI-Dokument, Free-Form GraphQL, ein Roh-SQL-Tool, einen uneingeschränkten Bucket, einen willkürlichen Dateisystem-Root, einen Shell-Befehl, einen Docker-Socket und implizite Belichtung jeder Operation ab, die ein Upstream-Upgrade hinzufügt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope MUST be a **default** client scope on every OIDC client that needs group-based RBAC. Making it optional reintroduces a userinfo regression: when optional with `include.in.token.scope=false`, Keycloak drops the group-membership mapper from userinfo even when the scope is explicitly requested, so consumers receive no groups and fall back to `subscriber`."
msgstr "Der Umfang muss ein **Ausfall** Kundenumfang für jeden OIDC-Client, der gruppenbasierte RBAC benötigt. Wenn Sie es optional machen, wird eine Userinfo-Regression wieder eingeführt: Wenn optional mit `include.in.token.scope=false`, Keycloak löscht den Gruppenmitgliedschafts-Mapper von userinfo, auch wenn der Umfang explizit angefordert wird, so dass Verbraucher keine Gruppen erhalten und auf `subscriber`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is image handling. Workflow orchestration, metadata resolution, and generic waiting logic should live in other script directories."
msgstr "Der Umfang dieses Ordners ist die Bildbearbeitung. Workflow-Orchestrierung, Metadatenauflösung und generische Wartelogik sollten in anderen Skriptverzeichnissen leben."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is installation and bootstrap. Lint execution, build workflows, and test orchestration should stay in their dedicated script directories."
msgstr "Der Umfang dieses Ordners ist Installation und Bootstrap. Lint-Ausführung, Build-Workflows und Test-Orchestrierung sollten in ihren dedizierten Skriptverzeichnissen bleiben."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is lint execution. Tool installation belongs in `scripts/install`, while build and test workflows should stay in their dedicated script directories."
msgstr "Der Umfang dieses Ordners ist die Ausführung von Flusen. Die Werkzeuginstallation gehört in `scripts/install`, während Build- und Test-Workflows in ihren dedizierten Skriptverzeichnissen bleiben sollten."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is missing-state resolution. Image build, release, and workflow orchestration should stay in their dedicated script or workflow locations."
msgstr "Der Umfang dieses Ordners ist die fehlende Zustandsauflösung. Image-Build, Release und Workflow-Orchestrierung sollten an ihren dedizierten Skript- oder Workflow-Speicherorten bleiben."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is script organization at the repository level. Detailed responsibilities belong in the README files of the respective subdirectories."
msgstr "Der Umfang dieses Ordners ist die Skriptorganisation auf Repository-Ebene. Detaillierte Verantwortlichkeiten gehören in die README-Dateien der jeweiligen Unterverzeichnisse."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is value resolution. Build, release, and wait-oriented behavior should stay in their dedicated script directories."
msgstr "Der Umfang dieses Ordners ist die Wertauflösung. Build, Release und warteorientiertes Verhalten sollten in ihren dedizierten Skriptverzeichnissen bleiben."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is waiting and availability checks. Build, release, and resource-specific lifecycle operations should stay in their dedicated directories."
msgstr "Der Umfang dieses Ordners ist Warten und Verfügbarkeitsprüfungen. Build-, Release- und ressourcenspezifische Lebenszyklusoperationen sollten in ihren dedizierten Verzeichnissen verbleiben."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "The script MUST act on the container through `container exec \"${GARBAGE_COLLECTOR_ADDRESS}\"`, using the application's native commands where they exist. Raw deletes are reserved for files the application cannot clean itself. It MUST NOT use host volume paths: a volume MAY be NFS or sit on another node."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script MUST be idempotent."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script MUST take exactly one argument, the mode: `routine` (daily timer) or `pressure` (the disc space cleaner found a full disk)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script first starts the role's deployed backup unit (a fresh differential generation of the live material), then mirrors each present subtree back to its fixed system path (`rsync -aHAX --delete`): `secrets` into `/var/lib/infinito/secrets`, `ca` into `/etc/<domain>/ca`, `acme` into `/etc/letsencrypt`, `certbot` into `/etc/certbot`. `--no-safety-backup` skips the pre-recover unit run. The `node` subtree (ssh host keys + machine-id) is restored only with `--restore-node-identity`, because overwriting the running machine-id / ssh host keys changes the host's identity mid-flight — do it on a fresh host after total loss."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script first starts the role’s deployed backup unit (a fresh differential generation of the live material), then mirrors each present subtree back to its fixed system path (``rsync -aHAX --delete``): ``secrets`` into ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets``, ``ca`` into ``/etc/<domain>/ca``, ``acme`` into ``/etc/letsencrypt``, ``certbot`` into ``/etc/certbot``. ``--no-safety-backup`` skips the pre-recover unit run. The ``node`` subtree (ssh host keys + machine-id) is restored only with ``--restore-node-identity``, because overwriting the running machine-id / ssh host keys changes the host’s identity mid-flight — do it on a fresh host after total loss."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script formats a disk only when all of these hold; otherwise the runner stays as it is:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script must stay free of every shell ``$``: the compose and swarm render paths launder dollars differently (a ``$pid`` reached the container as ``\"\"`` and crash-looped the sidecar on a sh syntax error). The bucket bootstrap therefore polls ``/status`` from a backgrounded subshell while ``exec`` makes the server PID 1; the poll loop dies with the container and readiness is gated by the consumer's bounded wait."
msgstr "Das Skript muss frei von jeder Shell bleiben ``$``: Der Kompositions- und Schwarm-Renderpfad wäscht Dollar unterschiedlich (a) ``$pid`` erreichte den Container als ``\"\"`` und crash-looped das Sidecar auf einem sh Syntaxfehler. Der Bucket Bootstrap führt daher zu Umfragen ``/status`` von einer Hintergrund-Subshell, während ``exec`` macht den Server PID 1; die Umfrageschleife stirbt mit dem Container und die Bereitschaft wird durch das begrenzte Warten des Verbrauchers eingeschränkt."

msgid "The script of a letter, not its codepoint range: ``ð`` and ``í`` are Latin and not ASCII, which is the difference between reading pseudo-Faroese as Latin text and reading it as something else."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script opens the LUKS device (interactive passphrase prompt; `--passphrase-stdin` for automation), mounts it, picks the newest device snapshot across every machine hash (a fresh host after total loss has a new machine id), mirrors it into the target (`rsync -aHAX --delete`) and unmounts/closes the device again. No pre-recover service backup runs: the device itself is the backup this role maintains. Afterwards restore individual applications from the backup root with the matching role's `recover.py` (`svc-bkp-volume-2-local` for docker volumes, `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local` for NFS exports)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script opens the LUKS device (interactive passphrase prompt; ``--passphrase-stdin`` for automation), mounts it, picks the newest device snapshot across every machine hash (a fresh host after total loss has a new machine id), mirrors it into the target (``rsync -aHAX --delete``) and unmounts/closes the device again. No pre-recover service backup runs: the device itself is the backup this role maintains. Afterwards restore individual applications from the backup root with the matching role’s ``recover.py`` (``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` for docker volumes, ``svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` for NFS exports)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script puts the swapfile on `/` when containerd already lives on `/mnt`, **prefers `/mnt`** otherwise when it is a separate partition (classic `ubuntu-latest` layout with `/dev/sdb` mounted at `/mnt`), and falls back to `/`. Current public runners no longer expose a separate `/mnt`, so the swapfile lands on `/` and must not starve the root filesystem."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The script type/extension (e.g., sh, py, yml)."
msgstr "Der Skripttyp/die Skripterweiterung (z. B. sh, py, yml)."

msgid "The script unpacks the archive into `custom_apps/.<app>.stage`, a directory Nextcloud skips because of its leading dot, and fails without touching the installed app when the archive lacks `<app>/appinfo/info.xml`."
