msgid "Where WordPress can certify a wildcard (no TLS, self-signed, or the Let's Encrypt `wildcard` flavor on a DNS challenge), one vhost serves `*.<parent>`, so a site is reachable as soon as the mapper creates it. Everywhere else every inventory user holding `site-owner` gets a vhost and a certificate for `<username>.<parent>`, and [tasks/05_site_owners.yml](tasks/05_site_owners.yml) reserves the site at deploy, administered by the deploy's administrator until the member's first sign-in claims it. A sign-in on a member host runs on the network's main site, whose auth cookie the network domain shares, so Keycloak needs no redirect URI per member. The SSO client settings come from the container on every site through `infinito-oidc-client`; no account opens or changes them, and the deploy deletes any stored copy."
