msgid "With `logout` disabled the administrator answers with `script-src-attr 'self'` (measured on the compose stack: response header of `/administrator/index.php`), so inline event handlers are blocked. Measured on the user and plugin lists: a click on the check-all box (`input[name=\"checkall-toggle\"]`, inline `onclick`) checks 0 rows and the browser reports a `script-src-attr` violation; the pagination links (`a.page-link`) carry inline `onclick` handlers too. `meta/csp.yml` allows `'unsafe-inline'` for `script-src-elem` and `style-src-attr` only, and `plugins/filter/csp_filters.py` adds it to `script-src-attr` solely when `logout` is enabled. Options: add `script-src-attr: unsafe-inline` to `meta/csp.yml`, or cover the path with a Playwright test first and decide then."
