msgid "[x] The provider maps display name, email, quota and groups from the claims, and the group claim provisions the RBAC groups the other plugins provision: `--mapping-display-name`, `--mapping-email`, `--mapping-quota`, `--mapping-groups` and `--group-provisioning=1` (`test_profile_quota_and_groups_come_from_the_claims`). With LDAP the administrator rights also hold through the existing path: the account is the `user_ldap` account, whose `ldap_admin_group` (`<application id>-administrator`) makes the role group Nextcloud's admins. In both modes the administrator group maps to `admin` the way `sociallogin` maps it (operator decision 2026-11-07, claim-driven): the own client carries the client role `admin` (`services.sso.oidc.client_roles` in `roles/web-app-nextcloud/meta/services.yml`), every deploy grants it to `/roles/web-app-nextcloud/administrator` (`kc_declared_client_role_grants` in `roles/web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/oidc_clients.py`, `roles/web-app-keycloak/tasks/update/16_client_role_grants.yml`), because the realm import holds no RBAC group below `/roles` to attach it to, and a multivalued `oidc-usermodel-client-role-mapper` on the client writes it into the groups claim. Upstream Keycloak 26.8.2 adds that role list to the group paths instead of replacing them (`AbstractUserRoleMappingMapper.java:111-116`, and `JsonUtils.mapClaim` at `server-spi-private/.../utils/JsonUtils.java:103-118` when the group mapper runs second, which forces `multivalued` at `GroupMembershipMapper.java:103`), and upstream `user_oidc` v8.12.0 takes a string claim value as the group id (`lib/Service/ProvisioningService.php:703`), keeps it unhashed with `--unique-uid=0` (`lib/Service/LocalIdService.php:20-40`), applies no whitelist when none is set (`:709-719`), joins the existing group through `createGroup` (`:856-866`, which returns an existing group at Nextcloud v34.0.0 `lib/private/Group/Manager.php:240-244`) and removes the user from every group the claim no longer names (`:846-853`). Proven by `TestNextcloudAdminClientRole` and `test_the_default_plugins_render_the_realm_byte_identically` in [test_backchannel_clients.py](../../tests/unit/python/roles/web-app-keycloak/templates/test_backchannel_clients.py), `TestDeclaredClientRoleGrants` in `tests/unit/python/roles/web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/test_oidc_clients.py`, and `test_the_admin_client_role_provisions_nextcloud_s_admin_group` with its negative control in `tests/unit/python/roles/web-app-nextcloud/test_user_oidc_provider.py`. The live sign-in belongs to the Playwright criterion below."
msgstr ""

